[00:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Hi. In this [music] video, I\'m going to show you a comparison between different reference modes using almost the same timeline and prompt. MSRV2 and ghost mask with only the background in the timeline. I also made a version with added images'

[00:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'key along with reference mode and also finally one with images guide and a global prompt only, so no prompt relay. Multiple backgrounds in MSR does not work. MSR only accepts one background in'

[00:24] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the timeline, so whether you put one or more won\'t change the final result. It is possible now to disable prompt relay in LTX director CS with a single toggle.'

[00:37] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Prompt relay, I believe, is not the best solution for any sequences. Prompt relay will prioritize prompt over images key and can easily bypass your image key, whereas with a single prompt, so prompt relay off, images keys have more'

[00:50] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'priority and a single prompt can work just as well depending on the complexity. So, for the test, the woman hears some footsteps from the T-Rex on a close-up shot, then run to the car, get inside, and drive with the camera facing'

[01:03] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the car from a low angle with the T-Rex behind chasing her. For those tests, honestly, I did several attempts when rendering without keyframes, but I will show you basically what to expect. This kind of prompt for'

[01:15] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'LTX without keyframes at all, only a background isn\'t optimal, but let\'s see. This is MSR mode V2 with a two times upscaler, Euler sampler for both as MSR works better with simple'

[01:29] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '&gt;&gt; [music] &gt;&gt; This one is ghost mask mode. No'

[01:42] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
