AUDIO: 'using Nano Banana. So, if you like what I do and want to support me in a way and get a potentially useful app, there is a link in the description. Now, let\'s analyze what went wrong with the MSRV2 version. Keep in mind, it is just an example, but'

[02:57] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'you are most likely to encounter those types of issues when using MSR ref mode. So, the background and the three refs are here and that is good considering there is nothing present in the timeline. But, all ref have their issue. First, the character face identity is of'

[03:11] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'court. It can be better, but it\'s never going to be perfect. Clothes, hairstyle are pretty close though. Then, the Jeep looks like the ref, but there are three handles per door and the back of the car is different and'

[03:23] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'perfectly clean, which is not the case in the ref sheet. In the final chase, the car looked quite a bit small. For the ghost mask mode without key frames, it is more or less the same issues. Colors are saturated, the car is perfectly clean [music] unlike the ref.'

[03:37] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'The face is not quite the same. Her hand reached the steering wheel too soon, but it is a one sequence shot as it is prompted in the global prompt. The T-Rex looks like a toy. Now, with key frames added and prompt relay on, I'

[03:50] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'found the result better. It is much easier [music] for LTX model to make a good animation when you help it with keyframes. So, we have the proper close-up face from the reference sheet, and the animation is segmented into shot because'

